company that is trying to scam you."
This was shockingly common, but,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:03.520
there wasn't much people could do.
They were negligent and slow, but,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:07.520
ASUS had all the power here.
The problem though, is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:12.080
every now and then, you stumble onto&nbsp;
someone who flips the power dynamic.&nbsp;

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:18.720
Just one year after the burning CPU scandal,&nbsp;
